{"chunk_id": "24abf93040ef", "text": "As Bhishma lies on his bed of arrows after being felled, he publicly praises Arjuna\u2019s unmatched prowess and warns Duryodhana that continuing the war will destroy the Kuru race. He urges peace while there is still time\u2014before Bhima, Yudhishthira, and the other Pandavas annihilate the Kaurava forces\u2014and even suggests returning half the kingdom. Duryodhana refuses the counsel, \u201clike a dying man rejecting medicine.\u201d Later Karna visits the wounded Bhishma. In a private, emotional exchange, Bhishma reveals he has always known Karna is Kunti\u2019s son and praises his valor, urging him to reconcile with the Pandavas, his brothers. Karna acknowledges the truth but refuses, bound by loyalty to Duryodhana and by fate. Bhishma reluctantly grants him permission to fight. The episode closes the Bhishma Parva, emphasizing tragic loyalty, destiny, and missed chances for peace.\nAfter Bhishma\u2019s fall, he urges Duryodhana to make peace and later reveals Karna\u2019s true birth, but Karna refuses and chooses loyalty to Duryodhana.\nThemes: loyalty versus blood ties, fate and destiny, war and reconciliation, honor of a kshatriya, tragic choice", "vector": [-0.004213446285575628, -0.015528973191976547, 0.00035403703805059195, 0.00417247274890542, -0.014108557254076004, 0.030675526708364487, -0.01734546758234501, -0.008201537653803825, -0.03856976330280304, -0.01275643054395914, 0.017837150022387505, 0.005019259173423052, 0.013739795424044132, 0.00936928391456604, -0.01294081099331379, -0.007750828750431538, 0.048020992428064346, 0.0008980035199783742, 0.03747713565826416, -0.03515530005097389, -0.00015791886835359037, 0.00213745329529047, -0.00909612700343132, 0.017277177423238754, -0.022275950759649277, 0.02467973157763481, 0.013295914977788925, -0.021292585879564285, 0.013207139447331429, -0.02674206718802452, -0.00692452909424901, 0.010161438956856728, -0.00011939946853090078, -0.004599280189722776, -0.02977410890161